⎿  KERN CLI UX Complete Redesign

Design Decisions (from User):

- Multi-cipher format: Grouped by input
- Language: English labels (consistent with flags)
- Colors: Infrastructure prepared, activation later
- Scope: Complete redesign with UI module

---
Phase 1: Create UI Module & Infrastructure

New file: src/ui/mod.rs
- Constants for symbols (arrows, tree chars, section separators)
- Formatting helpers (format_header, format_reduction_step, etc.)
- TTY detection and terminal width detection
- Color infrastructure (structs, theme system) - prepared but not activated
- Spacing rules as constants (SECTION_GAP = 2, etc.)

New file: src/ui/output.rs
- Dedicated output formatters for each mode:
  - format_reduce_result() - handles grouped multi-cipher
  - format_verbose_reduction() - clean trace output
  - format_lookup() - enhanced hierarchy
  - format_total() - simplified display
  - format_date() - unified format

---
Phase 2: Fix Critical Bugs

File: src/main.rs

1. Line 368, 366, 360: Replace all \u{1a} with proper Unicode →
2. Line 243: Add return; after date processing block
3. Line 166-243: Add lookup operation to date pipeline when flag set
4. Line 456: Remove "Keine weiteren Argumente angegeben." message entirely
5. Throughout: Standardize spacing (0/1/2 blank lines system)

---
Phase 3: Redesign All Output Formats

A. Reduce Output (lines ~320-330)

Single cipher:
test → 1 [ordinal]
example → 4 [ordinal]

Multiple ciphers (grouped):
test
  ordinal → 1
  pythagorean → 2
  chaldean → 4

example
  ordinal → 4
  pythagorean → 8
  chaldean → 6

B. Verbose Reduce (lines ~320-324)

Current:
test [ordinal]
test → [20+5+19+20] = 64
→ 6+4 = 10
→ Quersumme: 1

Redesign:
test [ordinal]
  20+5+19+20 = 64
  6+4 = 10
  1+0 = 1
  → 1
Remove redundant labels, clean hierarchy

C. Total Output (line ~368)

Simple:

Total: 11 → 2

Verbose:

Total Calculation
  1+4+6 = 11
  1+1 = 2
  → 2
Only show reduction if sum > 9

D. Lookup Output (lines ~394-441)

Standard:
1 · Origin, Will, Individuality, New Beginning
  └─ test [ordinal]

4 · Stability, Order, Structure, Security
  ├─ example [ordinal]
  └─ word [chaldean]
Note: Keep German bedeutung text, only labels English

With --full:
1 · Origin, Will, Individuality, New Beginning
  Sources:
    └─ test [ordinal]

  ⊕ Positive
    Pioniergeist, Führungsqualitäten, Mut zu neuen Wegen,
    Selbstvertrauen, Unabhängigkeit

  ⊖ Negative
    Egoismus, Sturheit, Dominanz, Rücksichtslosigkeit,
    Isolation durch Selbstüberschätzung

E. Date Output (lines ~226-237)

Simple:
+0 · 12.11.2025 → 5 [ordinal]
+1 · 13.11.2025 → 6 [ordinal]

Verbose:
+0 · 12.11.2025 [ordinal]
  1+2+1+1+2+0+2+5 = 14
  1+4 = 5
  → 5

+1 · 13.11.2025 [ordinal]
  ...

F. List Ciphers (lines ~118-126)

Current is good, minor alignment:
Available Ciphers:

  ordinal (or)            · Ordinal (A=1..Z=26)
  pythagorean (py)        · Pythagorean / Reduction
  chaldean (ch)           · Chaldean
  ...

---
Phase 4: Implement Spacing System

Rules:
- 0 lines: Related items (calculation steps, source list)
- 1 line: Between sections (results → total, entries in lookup)
- 2 lines: Before major section changes (reduce done → lookup starts)

Apply consistently throughout all output functions

